#: ../../../getstarted.md:1
msgid "Getting Started with Gazebo?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:3
msgid "Welcome to Gazebo!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:5
msgid ""
"To help you navigate our documentation, we have organized it into two "
"primary paths based on your workflow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:8
msgid ""
"**Users**: For those who primarily run Gazebo using standard tools (like `gz "
"sim`), edit SDFormat files, use existing plugins, and interact with running "
"simulations from the outside — typically by publishing and subscribing to "
"topics over Gazebo Transport or ROS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:12
msgid ""
"**Developers**: For those who use individual Gazebo libraries (like `gz-"
"math`, `sdformat`, or `gz-transport`) directly in their own C++ "
"applications, or those who are developing custom plugins for the simulator "
"(`gz-sim`) itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:17
msgid ""
"Regardless of which path fits you best, the first step is to get Gazebo "
"installed and running. Follow the steps below to set up your environment and "
"launch a test simulation, and then you can head to the sidebar to find "
"tutorials tailored to your role."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:23
msgid "Step 1: Install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:26
msgid ""
"If you are a [ROS](https://ros.org) user, please first read our tutorial on "
"[ROS/Gazebo installation](ros_installation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:29
msgid ""
"The recommended installation for new users is the use of binary packages "
"available for the platform to use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid "Platform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid "Gazebo Versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid "Ubuntu 24.04 Noble"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid ""
"[Gazebo Jetty](/docs/jetty/install_ubuntu){.external} (recommended), [Gazebo "
"Harmonic](/docs/harmonic/install_ubuntu){.external} (recommended if using "
"ROS 2 Jazzy) and [Gazebo Ionic](/docs/ionic/install_ubuntu){.external}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid "Ubuntu 22.04 Jammy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid ""
"[Gazebo Harmonic](/docs/harmonic/install_ubuntu){.external} (recommended) "
"and [Gazebo Fortress](/docs/fortress/install_ubuntu){.external} (recommended "
"if using ROS 2 Humble)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid "Mac Ventura"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid ""
"[Gazebo Harmonic](/docs/harmonic/install_osx){.external} (recommended) and "
"[Gazebo Fortress](/docs/fortress/install_osx){.external}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid "Mac Monterey"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:25
msgid ""
"Support via Conda-Forge is not fully functional, as there are known runtime "
"issues [see this issue for details](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/"
"issues/168)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:40
msgid ""
"If the desired platform is not listed above or if a particular feature in a "
"given [Gazebo release](releases) is needed, there is an installation package "
"per release available with all the installation options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:45
msgid ""
"[Gazebo Jetty installation](/docs/jetty/install){.external} options "
"(Expected: EOL 2031 May)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:46
msgid ""
"[Gazebo Ionic installation](/docs/ionic/install){.external} options (EOL "
"2026 Dec)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:47
msgid ""
"[Gazebo Harmonic (LTS) installation](/docs/harmonic/install){.external} "
"options (EOL 2029 May)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:48
msgid ""
"[Gazebo Fortress (LTS) installation](/docs/fortress/install){.external} "
"options (EOL 2027 May)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:50
msgid ""
"If you want to test the latest, unreleased Gazebo changes from `main`, see "
"the [Rotary release](/docs/rotary/rotary){.external} documentation. Rotary "
"is a rolling release intended for maintainers and early adopters; new users "
"should stick to one of the binary releases above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:55
msgid "Step 2: Run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:57
msgid ""
"After installing Gazebo in Step 1, you can launch Gazebo Sim, a 3D robotics "
"simulator, from a terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:60
msgid ""
"If you are on macOS, see specific instructions in the [macOS section]"
"(#macos)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:62
msgid "Launch Gazebo by running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:64
msgid ""
"gz sim shapes.sdf  # Fortress uses \"ign gazebo\" instead of \"gz sim\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:68
msgid ""
"This command will launch both the Sim server and Sim GUI with a world that "
"contains six simple shapes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:71
msgid ""
"Add the `-v 4` command line argument to generate error, warning, "
"informational, and debugging messages on the console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:74
msgid ""
"gz sim shapes.sdf -v 4  # Fortress uses \"ign gazebo\" instead of \"gz "
"sim\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:78
msgid ""
"Gazebo Sim can also be run headless, i.e. without the GUI, by using the `-s` "
"(server only) flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:80
msgid ""
"gz sim -s shapes.sdf -v 4  # Fortress uses \"ign gazebo\" instead of \"gz "
"sim\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:84
msgid ""
"Similarly, the GUI can be run independently using the `-g` (gui only) flag. "
"On start, the GUI will attempt to connect to a server instance. If a server "
"is not available, then you will see just a blank screen until a server "
"instances is started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:89
msgid "Step 3: Create your own world"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:91
msgid ""
"[SDF](http://sdformat.org/) is used to specify the contents of simulation. "
"Take a look at the available [SDF tutorials](http://sdformat.org/tutorials) "
"to get started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:95
msgid ""
"Modifying an existing SDF world is also a good way to get started. Gazebo "
"Sim ships with a number of [example SDF worlds](https://github.com/gazebosim/"
"gz-sim/blob/main/examples/worlds) that you can freely copy and modify. These "
"example SDF files are installed. Many of the SDF files also have "
"instructions located at the top of the SDF file. The instructions typically "
"contain information about how to run Sim with the SDF file in order to "
"experience a particular feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:103
msgid ""
"There are a wide variety of simulation resources at your disposal on "
"[https://app.gazebosim.org/fuel](https://app.gazebosim.org/fuel). If you "
"find a model you'd like to use, then click on the `<>` icon in the model "
"description page, highlighted in the image below, to copy an SDF snippet "
"into your clipboard. This snippet can be pasted directly into your custom "
"SDF file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:110
msgid "![SDF model snippet](images/model_snippet.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:110
msgid "SDF model snippet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:113
msgid "Step 4: Explore and learn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:115
msgid ""
"This tutorial has covered the basics of getting started with Gazebo. There "
"are more [versioned tutorials](/docs/citadel/tutorials){.external} covering "
"the basics of the GUI, creating worlds and robots, and more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:119
msgid ""
"Each [Gazebo library](/libs){.external} also has a set of tutorials and "
"examples. Explore these resources, and don't forget to ask questions and "
"find solutions at [answers.gazebosim.org](http://answers.gazebosim.org)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:123
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:125
msgid ""
"On macOS, you will need to run Gazebo using two terminals, one for the "
"server and another for the GUI:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:128
msgid ""
"# launch server in one terminal\n"
"gz sim -v 4 shapes.sdf -s  # Fortress uses \"ign gazebo\" instead of \"gz "
"sim\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:133
msgid ""
"# launch gui in a separate terminal\n"
"gz sim -v 4 -g  # Fortress uses \"ign gazebo\" instead of \"gz sim\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getstarted.md:138
msgid ""
"The GUI on macOS is currently known to be unstable. Basic interaction with "
"the 3D scene such as camera view control and translation / rotation tools "
"should be functional. However, some GUI plugins like the Component Inspector "
"may be buggy and interaction with certain GUI elements may cause the GUI to "
"crash. Please ticket an issue at https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/ if you "
"run into GUI problems on macOS."
msgstr ""
